Z||000000||My7Fieros||07-12-2000||03:22 AM||||1. The clearcoat is comming off my Gt wheels..how do I get the rest off, get that "machined look", and what kind of clearcoat to put on?<BR>2. What causes the front brakes (only) to stay locked tight? Ive rebuilt the calipers and changed the pads...there dosnt appear to be a bent line........proportion valve maybe?<BR>TIA, Brian<P>umm..is that 2 question? lol<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-12-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000001||lennyb4||07-12-2000||08:23 AM||||M7F... There has been alot of very detailed information covering wheel refinishing. Try doing a search in Tech. Discussion for the info. It basiclly involves using permatex spray on gasget remover, a brass brush, and other various items. ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Oreif||07-12-2000||10:51 AM||||Here is the thread for when I refinished my GT style wheels.<BR>For clearcoat I used "Dupli-color Clear urethane wheel paint" most AutoZones and Trak Auto carry it.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/002367.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/002367.html</A> <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-12-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000003||theogre||07-12-2000||12:19 PM||||rubber brake lines can be bad inside, that could do this.<P>the prop valve works on the back brakes. It wouldn't do this. Rust in the prop/balance block however could. If a chunk of rust has gotten jammed in the block, a line, or even the master cyl port, then it could be acting like a check valve blocking release.||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||07-12-2000||05:29 PM||||Great..thanx for the help guys!||||reg||7
